CHAPTER VI
INSTITUTION FOR THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR VICTIMS Article 13 (1) The Regional Government establishes an Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children (P2TP2A) as the Implementing Institution for Prevention and Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence in an integrated manner.
(2) P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements of:
a. health;
b. law enforcement;
c. social affairs and empowerment;
d. education and religious affairs;
e. Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs); and
f. private sector.
(3) Further provisions regarding P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

